| Goal ID | Goal Title                 | Text                                                         | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
| ------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------ | --------- | -------- |
| G1      | Deliver Resources to Requesting Agent | Ensure resources are collected from storage and delivered to the requesting agent's location. | -                  | Achieve   | -        |
| G2      | Collect Resources          | Retrieve all required resources from designated storage locations. | #                  | Achieve   | G1       |
| G3      | Deliver Resources          | Transport all collected resources to the requesting agent's specified location. | ;                  | Achieve   | G1       |
| G4      | Navigate to Storage        | Move the robot to the specified storage location for resource retrieval. | -                  | Perform   | G2       |
| G5      | Request Resource Retrieval | Send a message to the storage requesting the specific resource and wait for retrieval. | -                  | Perform   | G2       |
| G6      | Return to Recharging Station | If battery drops to 10% during collection, return to the recharging station. | FALLBACK(G4, G7)   | Perform   | G2       |
| G7      | Assign Task to Another Robot | If battery is low, assign the remaining collection task to another robot. | -                  | Perform   | G6       |
| G8      | Transport Resource         | Deliver the retrieved resource to the requesting agent's location. | -                  | Perform   | G3       |
| G9      | Return to Checkpoint       | If battery drops to 30% during delivery, return to a checkpoint. | FALLBACK(G8, G10)  | Perform   | G3       |
| G10     | Assign Delivery Task to Another Robot | If resource cannot be returned to checkpoint, assign remaining task to another robot. | -                  | Perform   | G9       |
| G11     | Alert Sector Manager       | If resource fails to return to checkpoint, trigger an alert and report to the sector manager. | -                  | Achieve   | G9       |

| Task ID | Task Title             | Text                                           | Relation | Location          | Number of Robots |
| ------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | -------- | ----------------- | ---------------- |
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage    | Move the robot to the designated storage location. | AND      | Storage           | 1                |
| AT2     | Request Resource       | Send a message to the storage requesting the resource. | AND      | Storage           | 1                |
| AT3     | Return to Recharge     | Return to the recharging station and charge.   | AND      | Recharging Station | 1               |
| AT4     | Assign Task            | Transfer the remaining collection task to another robot. | AND      | Control Center    | 1                |
| AT5     | Deliver Resource       | Transport the resource to the requesting agent's location. | AND      | Requesting Location | 1              |
| AT6     | Return to Checkpoint   | Return the resource to a designated checkpoint. | AND      | Checkpoint        | 1                |
| AT7     | Assign Delivery Task   | Transfer the remaining delivery task to another robot. | AND      | Control Center    | 1                |
| AT8     | Alert Sector Manager   | Send an alert and report to the sector manager. | AND      | Control Center    | 1                |

**Logical Relationships:**

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND;]** (Sequential execution of collection followed by delivery)
- **G2 -> G4, G5, G6 [AND#]** (Parallel execution of navigation, request, and fallback for low battery)
- **G6 -> G4, G7 [FALLBACK]** (Fallback: if battery is low, return to charge or assign task)
- **G3 -> G8, G9 [AND;]** (Sequential delivery steps with fallback for low battery)
- **G9 -> G8, G10, G11 [FALLBACK]** (Fallback: if checkpoint fails, alert sector manager)
- **G2.1 (Collect Resource A) -> AT1, AT2 [AND]** (Navigation and request tasks for one storage)
- **G2.2 (Collect Resource B) -> AT1, AT2 [AND]** (Parallel execution for another storage)
- **G3 -> AT5 [AND]** (Delivery task for the resource)
- **G9 -> AT6, AT7, AT8 [FALLBACK]** (Fallback delivery steps)

**Summary:**
The goal model ensures that resources are collected from storages in parallel (if multiple robots are assigned) and delivered sequentially. Battery checks trigger fallbacks to recharging or task reassignment. Delivery phase includes checkpoint returns and alerts if necessary. Tasks are assigned to individual robots with specific locations and actions.
